# The CLI uploads the working directory, and without this it sends the whole
# monorepo -- 460MB of dependencies and build output, which fails the 100MB
# limit. Vercel installs and builds from source on its own machines, so none
# of this is wanted there.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.next
**/.next
.turbo
**/.turbo
dist
**/dist
coverage
**/coverage
.git
*.log
.env.local

# The self-hosted image's build files (Oracle box: .github/workflows/
# images.yml). Vercel must never receive a Dockerfile: with one at the root
# of the upload, every deploy of these projects fails at "Deploying
# outputs..." with
#   Cannot patch preview comments when immutable static file upload is
#   enabled. Upgrade to next@v16.3.0-canary.32 or newer to resolve this.
#   (errorCode IMMUTABLE_STATIC_PATCH_PREVIEW_COMMENTS)
# -- although Next here is newer than that. Proven on 2026-10-24: the same
# commit failed with the Dockerfile uploaded and was READY without it. The
# image build is unaffected: Docker reads the Dockerfile from the
# repository, never through this file.
Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile
*.Dockerfile
.dockerignore
deploy/build
